    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I would say if you are just getting start in R entirely to start with the R for DataScience book. It&#39;s the most recent book and has elements of getting data into R, changing it to the right format, analyzing it, and visualizing it. There is a good basic ggplot2 chapter in it and it is available online for free. <div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://r4ds.had.co.nz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r4ds.had.co.nz/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367324047000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Or3_CAKoisfvjNDxA9toj\">http://r4ds.had.co.nz/</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>HTH, </div><div>B</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
